# The same mistake as in fix_stable_exp.txtar, but on a file which the
# module's language version cannot parse at all: the old prefix alias
# syntax is what aliasv2 replaced, so nothing loads. Both the stable
# experiment and the load failure are reported, rather than the package
# being passed over in silence for having no files the fixer can see.
! exec cue fix --exp=aliasv2 .
cmp stderr expect/stderr
cmp a.cue expect/a

# Every other command reports the load failure too.
! exec cue vet .
stderr 'old-style alias syntax'

-- cue.mod/module.cue --
module: "mod.test"

language: version: "v0.18.0"
-- a.cue --
package p

X=a: 1
b:   X
-- expect/a --
package p

X=a: 1
b:   X
-- expect/stderr --
fix: experiment "aliasv2" is already stable as of language version v0.18.0; files at this version use it without an attribute
old-style alias syntax (=) is not allowed as of language version v0.18.0; use postfix syntax (~X or ~(K,V)):
    ./a.cue:3:2
